  "record_ids": [],
  "asserts_no_claim": true,
  "purpose": "Bind the zero-entry decay control and the S-box arm by hash before any reviewer reads them.",
  "outcomes_as_reported": {
    "RANK_1_decay_control": "THE r=5 HALF SURVIVES AND THE FALSIFICATION PATTERN DID NOT FIRE. Trials reading n mod 8 = 0 out of 40 (chance 5): r=4 gives 40/40/40, r=5 gives 40/40/40, r=6 gives 4 (no-zero control) / 9 (Z1) / 7 (Z4), r=7 gives 7/5/5. F1 required >=36 at r=6 under a zero-entry layer with the control at <=15; observed 9 and 7. DECAY TRACKS ROUND COUNT, NOT ZERO ENTRIES.",
    "RANK_1_mechanism": "The GF(2^8) fiber signature reproduces in the nibble analogue EXACTLY under 256 -> 16. And the degeneracy DIES: all-fibers-divisible holds 40/40 at r=4 and r=5, then 0/40 at r=6 and r=7. THE STRONGEST SINGLE ARM: Z1 at r=5 forces the residue with NO degeneracy at all -- gcd of nonzero fibers is 1 on 40/40, max_occ 7-9 -- which was the load-bearing supposition of the OBS-B3-4 worry.",
    "RANK_1_three_batch_old_item_filled": "BATCH-001's substitute circulant is CONFIRMED SINGULAR (det 0 by two independent methods, rank 3), and recompiling that batch's own mini.c unmodified reproduced its 'MC singular' refusal. The abort was correct behaviour, not a bug. 12660 of 13500 one-zero circulants are non-singular, so it was an unlucky draw.",
    "RANK_1_producer_self_correction": "Its preregistration predicted Z1/Z4 near chance at r=4 and measured 40/40. It recorded the error rather than dropping it. What actually breaks at r=4 is the EXACT-ZERO result (n=0: 40/40 under the control, 0/40 under Z1/Z4), which is what the r=4 half of CORR-20260802-46b73b says. The error does not touch the F1/F2 rule, which references only r=5 and r=6.",
    "RANK_3_the_scoping_result": "S-BOX-INDEPENDENT. The r=5 yoyo survives uniformly random bijective S-boxes: AES 13.5x, random draw 1 11.0x, random draw 2 20.5x, all at 2^31 trials against a null of 2.0 with one-sided p below 1e-15. The reference arm reproduced BATCH-002's 15.63x at 13.5x in a THIRD independent implementation, inside the frozen 8x-25x band, so the random arms are interpretable. COMBINED WITH THE ALREADY-ESTABLISHED S-BOX-INDEPENDENCE OF THE COUNTING PROPERTIES, NOTHING THIS CAMPAIGN HAS FOUND IS SPECIFIC TO AES.",
    "RANK_3_rewritten_not_reused": "BATCH-002's probe uses AES-NI, which hardwires the S-box in silicon and makes substitution impossible. The producer wrote a T-table software AES with a run-time S-box parameter, pinned by FIPS-197 C.1 and 5120 round-trips at 0 failures, with each random S-box passing the round-trip pin in place of the inapplicable KAT. Random S-boxes built by Fisher-Yates with rejection sampling, bijectivity verified by the binary before measuring.",
    "RANK_3_control_breach_recorded_not_softened": "Y-R2-sd fell OUTSIDE its preregistered <=2.5x structure-destroyed band at 4.0x (4 hits vs null 1.0). It is nowhere near the ALIVE bar (p = 0.019 against a required 1e-6) and reads as an ordinary upward fluctuation at 2^30, but the producer flagged it as a reason to re-run the controls at higher trial counts before anyone leans on them. Its controls ran at 2^30, not BATCH-002's 2^32, declared in advance and budget-driven.",
    "RANK_2_positive_control_PASSES": "The same sq_slot binary (source sha256 byte-identical to BATCH-003's) with slotmask=0, every hint byte from the TRUE key schedule, returns {1: 4}: all four diagonals unique and each survivor equal to the true byte. THE ALL-EMPTY REGRESSION HYPOTHESIS IS EXCLUDED, so BATCH-003 rank 4's {0:4} readings are not an artifact of a dead binary."
  },
  "what_remains_open": {
    "OBS_B3_4_at_byte_width": "OPEN. The decay control is a GF(2^4) ANALOGUE. It removes one specific reason to disbelieve the r=5 half, in an instrument that demonstrably shows the same signature, but it does NOT close the byte-width gap. The GF(2^8) M0/M1 arm at r=6 stays queued.",
    "what_the_S_box_arm_does_not_establish": "Two draws bound very little about 256! bijections: the result says those two draws preserved the signal, not that every bijection does.",
    "structure_destroyed_controls": "Should be re-run at 2^32 before anyone leans on them, per the producer's own flag."
  },
